      "status": "shadow",
      "_known_differences": [
        "Finding 19: the composition defines net income before shelter twice. The final net income uses `medical_deduction`, which applies Colorado's $165 SMD (7 CFR 273.9(d)(3)); the shelter cost uses `snap_net_income_before_shelter`, whose medical term is the plain max(0, medical - 35). PE applies the SMD consistently, so the shelter deduction differs by half the medical difference. Internal inconsistency upstream in rulespec-us, not a mapping error.",
        "Finding 20: the composition rounds to whole dollars (floor(x+0.5)) and floors the earned-income deduction per 273.10(e)(1)(i)(B); PE keeps cents. Bounds the residual at about $1. Rounding-policy decision, not a defect."
      ]
    },
    {
      "pe_variable": "snap_net_income",
      "axiom_output": "snap_net_income",
      "status": "shadow",
      "_known_differences": [
        "Finding 21: the composition subtracts child support twice - once via snap_income_exclusions inside snap_total_gross_income, then again in snap_net_income_pre_shelter. Colorado excludes it from gross under 7 CFR 273.9(d)(5); exclusion or deduction, never both. PE does it once. The gap equals the child-support amount exactly on all 125 differing Colorado units. No manifest-side fix: presuming the verification gate false would also zero the gross-income exclusion and break gross income. Fix upstream in rulespec-us."
      ]
